  "Main topic of the publication": "This paper investigates the similarities in DNA methylation patterns between the placenta and cancers, suggesting that common epigenetic mechanisms may regulate behaviors such as tissue invasion, angiogenesis, and immune system evasion. The study identifies megabase-scale patterns of hypomethylation in the early pregnancy placenta that mirror those in tumors, potentially leading to biomarkers and drug targets in oncology, obstetrics, and gynecology.",
